From f5ee1fa6a79e6b10dbe5e2ea7204b09f9075c3fe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 18 Jun 2026 11:36:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/51] begonia-wifi (fwport): in-kernel srh_patch (multi-patch
 / connac MCU patch)

After srh_rom_patch loaded the EMI firmware and the conn started replying
(hw_check now reads chip id 0x6785 ok), mtk_wcn_soc_sw_init advanced to the
multi-patch download and hit the SAME userspace-launcher gap: wmt_ctrl_patch_search
issued ul_cmd("srh_patch") to the absent stp_uart_launcher -> timeout ->
patch info prepare fail(-1) -> sw_init fail(-6).

Replay the launcher srh_patch in-kernel (wmt_dev_srh_patch_headless): verify the
MCU patch (soc1_0_patch_mcu_2a_1_hdr.bin) is present, then publish patchNum=1 and
a WMT_PATCH_INFO whose PDA target is CONNAC_PATCH_START_ADDR (0x0001C000, per
begonia gen4m connac.h/connac2x2.h; patch u4PatchVer 0x0001c0xx corroborates),
reusing the existing pPatchInfo/pAtchNum statics + free path.

Signed-off-by: Michal Andrzejczak <mit.mis@gmail.com>
